[I]Reading: on Spigot the platform-wide chunk-gen ceiling caps everyone at 3.5–4.5 TPS during the burst, but the [B]MSPT spike[/B] tells you who is parking the main thread. RTP-Pro's queued, off-tick path keeps the worst tick at [B]3 ms[/B] — a non-event — while BetterRTP and HuskHomes drive single ticks past 3.7 s, the sort of spike that causes player rubber-banding and watchdog warnings. † JakesRTP ran in slot 4 of a 4-phase chain on Spigot, so its Min TPS / CPU-per-TP figures are confounded by carry-over from the prior HuskHomes phase and are withheld until a slot-1 (or solo) rerun; the dispatch-time numbers (throughput, p99) are reported because they measure per-attempt work, not accumulated server state.[/I]

[B]Folia 1.21.11[/B]
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Plugin[/TH][TH]Throughput (TP/s)[/TH][TH]Region MSPT p99 (ms)[/TH][TH]Success[/TH][TH]CPU / TP (ms)[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]🧪 RTP-Pro[/B][/TD][TD][B]9.87[/B][/TD][TD][B]157[/B][/TD][TD][B]99.97 %[/B][/TD][TD][B]18.0[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]🧪 BetterRTP[/TD][TD]3.82[/TD][TD]1 200[/TD][TD]100 %[/TD][TD]34.8[/TD][/TR]
