[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#C0392B]Support Policy[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Support is for bugs and configuration questions,[/B] after you've read the admin guide linked above and the in-repo wiki.
[*][B]Bug reports need a reproduction:[/B] server version, plugin version, platform (Spigot, Paper, or Folia), attached `config.yml`, `regions/`, and `safety.yml`, plus the relevant `server.log` section. Reports without these will be asked for them once, then closed.
[*][B]"It doesn't work" is not a bug report.[/B] Neither is "it's broken on my server." Tell me what you did, what you expected, and what actually happened instead.
[*][B]Unsupported scenarios include[/B] Fabric (planned for a later release), Forge / NeoForge except via Arclight or Mohist (both officially supported), plugin conflicts I can't reproduce, and general Minecraft-server administration questions. For that last one, the SpigotMC help forum is the right venue.
[*][B]Response time:[/B] I'm a solo maintainer. Expect 24 to 72 hours on weekdays for properly-filed reports. Critical safety issues (S-001 through S-007 violations) jump the queue.
[*][B]Feature requests[/B] are welcome via GitHub issues, not the resource discussion thread. Priority is driven by the published roadmap, not ticket volume.
[/LIST]

This policy exists because focused engineering time is what keeps the plugin fast and current. Respecting it is how you get the most out of your purchase.

[CENTER][COLOR=#D1D1D1]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#C0392B]Support Philosophy[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[QUOTE]
I'm a solo engineer maintaining a deterministic, high-performance teleport engine. Instead of padding this resource with cosmetic bloat, my development time stays focused on Folia concurrency and zero-latency execution.

Choose RTP if you care about engineering quality, RAM efficiency, and compounding TPS stability more than you care about feature-padding and GUI gimmicks.
[/QUOTE]

